   "en": {
    "headline": "Google will turn off Search in schools that don't want its AI features",
    "summary_short": "On school accounts, Gemini and Google Search will come bundled: AI can't be removed without losing search too. Schools that reject AI will be left without Google Search.",
    "summary_long": "Google has announced that Gemini, Gemini Notebook, Gemini in Classroom and Google Search will be off by default on K-12 student accounts. They will only work if school administrators turn them on. But administrators can't enable Search while leaving out the Gemini features: it's all or nothing.\n\nChris Phillips, Google's vice president of education, explained it to The New York Times: \"Search and AI are deeply integrated.\" The consequence is that a school that doesn't want AI for its students also loses the search engine. The news sparked a broad debate on Hacker News, with more than 400 comments.",
    "unconfirmed_claims": []
